Thoughtful concern. Let me actually think about this rather than handwave.

Atomic refcount cost: on x86, `lock xadd` is ~10-20ns uncontended. On ARM with LL/SC, similar order. A parser that clones a token per call, across say 100k tokens, is 10k * 20ns = 200μs total. Probably a rounding error next to the parsing itself.

